From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: valentin rameau <valentin.rameau@outlook.fr>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:37:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 11/33] Record LLE arrivals into the raster handler region

The Vita host enters $00:8601 only through the generated alias, so any
interpreted step arriving in $00:8601-$00:8680 from outside that range came by
another route. Report the step that jumped there and the M/X/E the arrival
carries, since the bands require M=8/X=16 and an entry that skips $8601's
REP #$10 mis-decodes their LDX #imm by one byte.

Vita-only, inside the existing #ifdef VITA step hook.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c b/runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c
index ebdaf4e..48eae3e 100644
--- a/runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c
+++ b/runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c
@@ -1844,6 +1844,25 @@ static int _interp_run_core(CpuState *cpu, uint32_t entry_pc24,
               if (s_prev_mapped && !_mapped)
                 interp_bridge_note_offrails_vita(s_prev_pc, s_prev_op, s_prev_sp,
                                                  pc_before, op);
+              /* Entries into the raster handler region $00:8601-$00:8680.
+               * The host enters it only through bank_00_8601's AOT alias, so
+               * an LLE step arriving here from outside names whatever other
+               * route reaches it -- and carries the width it arrives with,
+               * which is the thing that decodes the bands wrong. */
+              { extern void interp_bridge_note_irq_entry_vita(
+                    uint32_t from_pc, uint8_t from_op, uint32_t pc,
+                    uint16_t sp, uint8_t mf, uint8_t xf, uint8_t e);
+                int _in_irq_region = (pc_before >= 0x008601u &&
+                                      pc_before <= 0x008680u);
+                int _was_in = (s_prev_pc >= 0x008601u &&
+                               s_prev_pc <= 0x008680u);
+                if (_in_irq_region && !_was_in)
+                  interp_bridge_note_irq_entry_vita(s_prev_pc, s_prev_op,
+                                                    pc_before, in.sp,
+                                                    (uint8_t)(in.mf ? 1 : 0),
+                                                    (uint8_t)(in.xf ? 1 : 0),
+                                                    (uint8_t)(in.e ? 1 : 0));
+              }
               s_prev_pc = pc_before; s_prev_op = op; s_prev_sp = in.sp;
               s_prev_mapped = _mapped;
             }
